{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"I smoke-tested it against real opencode 1.18.5 rather than just reading it. Verdict: **the structural reverse-engineering is largely right, but fabrication fails on any conversation containing a tool call — i.e. essentially every real coding conversation.** Details below, with what I actually ran.\n\n## Blockers (verified, not speculative)\n\n**1. Tool parts fail import — hard stop.** I fabricated a conversation with one `tool_use`/`tool_result` pair and ran the adapter end-to-end:\n\n```\nopencode import failed: Error: Unexpected error\nMissing key at [\"state\"][\"title\"]\n```\n\nBisecting the schema, `state` requires **`status`, `input`, `output`, `title`, `metadata`, `time`** — the adapter emits only the first three. Adding `title`, `metadata: {}`, and `time: {start,end}` made import succeed on the first try. Text-only conversations import and render fine, which is presumably why the model thought it worked.\n\n**2. Failed imports are not atomic and don't fall back.** The failing run still left a half-imported session (3 of 4 messages) in the user's opencode DB, listed in the picker. Worse, `fabricate` throws a plain `Error`, not `FabricationUnsupportedError`, so `buildPlan` in `src/resume.ts:134` rethrows instead of degrading to bootstrap — the user gets a stack trace and a corrupt session instead of the documented recovery path.\n\n**3. The shim is inverted and recurses.** `src/shim.ts:52` triggers on `$# -eq 2`, so `opencode -s <id>` is intercepted and **the session id is silently dropped**, while the bare gesture it claims to catch passes through. I ran the branch logic directly:\n\n```\n./shim -s ses_abc123     → INTERCEPTED (args dropped)\n./shim -s                → PASSTHROUGH\n```\n\nSince `nativeResume` launches `opencode -s <id>` through PATH — where the shim wins — this is an infinite loop: shim → picker → `opencode -s` → shim. The claude/codex shims both guard with `$# -eq 1`. Honestly, opencode has no bare \"open the picker\" invocation equivalent to `claude --resume`, so I'd drop the opencode shim entirely rather than invent a trigger.\n\n## Correctness issues\n\n**4. The import notice lands last and renders as `QUEUED`.** I launched the fabricated session under the repo's own pty harness (`scripts/pty-run.exp`). Markers rendered, but opencode orders by `time.created`, and the notice is stamped at fabrication time — which is always ≥ every real event — so it sorts to the *end*, where a trailing user message with no reply shows as a queued prompt. This is guaranteed, not incidental. Backdate the notice to just before the first event.\n\n**5. `parentID` semantics are wrong.** Real export: user messages have *no* `parentID`; each assistant message points at the user message that prompted it (several assistants share one parent). The adapter builds a linear chain, so user messages get parented to assistant messages.\n\n**6. `projectID: \"global\"`** — real sessions carry a per-directory hash. Confirmed consequence: fabricated sessions appear in `opencode session list` from *every* directory, unlike native ones.\n\n**7. Violates the fabrication contract in `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:83`** (\"propagate the source model id verbatim … never substitute a recognized-but-false id\"). The adapter hardcodes `providerID: \"turnbridge\"` / `modelID: \"turnbridge-import\"` and never reads `event.actor.id` the way `claude-code.ts:196` does.\n\n**8. Tool output is discarded then duplicated.** `state.output` is hardcoded to `\"[historical tool call — not re-executed]\"` even though the real result arrives in the next block — which is then folded in again as loose `[tool result]` text. `seenCallIds` is populated and never read, so the pairing work is dead code. opencode's tool part has a real `output` field; use it.\n\n**9. `_opts.replayReasoning` is ignored.** Thinking blocks always become native `reasoning` parts, bypassing the flag and the config switch. Codex deliberately gates this and only replays *native*-origin reasoning.\n\n## Convention gaps\n\n- `VALIDATED_VERSION_PREFIX = \"1.\"` claims validation that doesn't hold (1.18.5 fails on tools), and `\"1.\"` would match 1.x forever — codex pins to two minors. `scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs` wasn't given an opencode entry, so drift silently ignores it (package is `opencode-ai`, latest 1.18.11).\n- No `docs/specs/opencode-*.md`, while the drift report links a spec per target.\n- **Zero tests.** `buildImportPayload` isn't exported, so it can't be tested without launching opencode — the other two adapters export `buildRolloutLines`/`buildSessionLines` precisely so `fabricate-invariants.test.ts` can exercise them. This is the root cause of the whole list: nothing forced the payload to be inspected. `scripts/smoke-interactive.mjs:189` also still hardcodes `[\"claude-code\", \"codex\"]`, and the README wasn't updated.\n- **No ledger capture path.** `conversation-ledger` has no opencode adapter (its README lists it as SQLite/plugin-API, unimplemented), so this is a one-way bridge: turns made in opencode are never captured, and the `fabricatedConversationId` lineage points at a conversation that will never reappear. Not necessarily wrong as a first step, but the PR doesn't say so, and the roadmap explicitly says \"deepen the two existing targets before broadening.\"\n\n## What it got right\n\nCommand surface (`-s <id>`, `import <file>`), the export/import envelope shape, the `Imported session: <id>` stdout regex (exact match, and re-import is idempotent), the picker-title convention, text/reasoning part shapes, and the tool-call-as-history framing. That's genuinely non-trivial reverse-engineering for a one-shot. The failure mode is characteristic: it inferred the format from the happy path and never validated the branch it couldn't see.\n\nSanity check on my own claims: build and all 77 existing tests pass on the branch (none touch opencode). I cleaned up after myself — deleted the three fabricated smoke sessions plus the orphan the failed import left behind, and removed `~/.turnbridge/imports/`; your original opencode session is untouched. I made no code changes and posted nothing to GitHub.\n\nresult: PR #3 reviewed and smoke-tested against opencode 1.18.5 — fabrication is broken for any conversation with a tool call (`state` requires `title`/`metadata`/`time`), failures leave partial sessions with no bootstrap fallback, and the shim hijacks `opencode -s <id>` into an infinite loop; 9 further correctness/convention issues listed, format reverse-engineering otherwise solid.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"feature/opencode-target","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"0d3d8beda8f2882af0a11a82fc3af34b332e2a7d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","seq":161},"id":"ev1-981b2db9e2fdb7bf0581b1cab5318d57f5d4e26fc196cd0809f95c6946e21b42","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-02T16:57:28.229Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"feature/opencode-target","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"I smoke-tested it against real opencode 1.18.5 rather than just reading it. Verdict: **the structural reverse-engineering is largely right, but fabrication fails on any conversation containing a tool call — i.e. essentially every real coding conversation.** Details below, with what I actually ran.\n\n## Blockers (verified, not speculative)\n\n**1. Tool parts fail import — hard stop.** I fabricated a conversation with one `tool_use`/`tool_result` pair and ran the adapter end-to-end:\n\n```\nopencode import failed: Error: Unexpecte